commit 3c3cb02a
author: cdvankammen
date: 2026-10-24 07:24:24 -0600
subject: feat(security): OIDC save-time validation gate on /api/settings PATCH

Prevents persisting an unreachable/malformed OIDC issuer when authMode would

disable password login (the evil.example.com scenario from Finding #13).

- New validateOidcConfigForSave() in src/lib/auth/oidc.js: 5s-timeout discovery

  fetch; rejects unreachable hosts, non-HTTPS (except localhost), malformed URLs,

  non-JSON responses, and discovery docs missing authorization_endpoint /

  token_endpoint.

- fetchOidcDiscovery() now accepts {signal} for AbortController wiring.

- settings/route.js: hard gate when effective authMode disables password login

  ('oidc' or 'sso'+oidc); soft probe (URL+HTTPS only, no network) otherwise.

- Escape hatch: skipOidcValidation:true in body (never persisted).

- 'both' mode never hard-gated (password login stays enabled).

- 'saml' mode excluded (own config surface, no OIDC discovery).

- 13 unit tests in tests/unit/oidc-save-validation.test.js, all passing.

